<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 4 November, from 1333 to 2008.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/florence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1333 CE <span class="tih-ago">693 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Arno floods Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After days of heavy rain, the Arno burst its banks and swept away three of Florence's four bridges, including the Ponte Vecchio. The chronicler Giovanni Villani recorded the disaster in detail.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The poet Wilfred Owen is killed in action</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wilfred Owen was killed crossing the Sambre-Oise Canal in France, a week before the armistice. His poems, including 'Dulce et Decorum Est', became the defining English verse of the First World War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1922 CE <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howard Carter finds the steps to Tutankhamun's tomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Howard Carter's workers uncovered a step cut into the rock of the Valley of the Kings, leading to the nearly intact tomb of Tutankhamun. Its treasures caused a worldwide sensation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1956 CE <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet tanks move in to crush the Hungarian Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces launched a massive assault on Budapest at dawn, overthrowing Imre Nagy's government. Thousands were killed, and the West did not intervene.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1979 CE <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Students seize the US embassy in Tehran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Iranian students occupied the US embassy in Tehran and took 66 hostages. Fifty-two were held for 444 days, a crisis that soured US-Iranian relations and damaged Jimmy Carter's presidency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2008 CE <span class="tih-ago">18 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Barack Obama is elected president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Barack Obama defeated John McCain to become the first African American elected president of the United States, 45 years after Martin Luther King's 'I Have a Dream' speech.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
